1
00:00:25,043 --> 00:00:26,223
How about you?

2
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:27,561
Feel like fighting?

3
00:00:28,243 --> 00:00:29,463
No thanks, pal.

4
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:34,081
My magic skill's gonna reach 900
soon, so I'd rather not die just yet.

5
00:00:34,563 --> 00:00:35,940
At least you're honest about it.

6
00:00:36,023 --> 00:00:37,199
How about you, miss?

7
00:00:39,563 --> 00:00:40,760
Guess I'll pass, too.

8
00:00:40,843 --> 00:00:43,223
But next time, you're going down! Oh.

9
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:47,054
Then next time, I'll make sure
to bring more friends along.

10
00:01:26,263 --> 00:01:28,040
I can't see the future!

11
00:01:28,123 --> 00:01:34,140
I can't see the next time!

12
00:01:34,223 --> 00:01:36,620
I'm still a word.

13
00:01:36,703 --> 00:01:37,533
I'm still a word.

14
00:01:37,616 --> 00:01:39,280
I'm still a word. I'm still a

15
00:01:39,363 --> 00:01:46,363
word.

16
00:02:24,203 --> 00:02:25,033
You?

17
00:02:25,116 --> 00:02:25,946
Hey,

18
00:02:26,029 --> 00:02:28,080
what's up with those
flames there remain lights

19
00:02:28,163 --> 00:02:30,634
the players who killed can still hear you?

20
00:02:33,623 --> 00:02:39,000
Okay, now we can talk so what do you
want you want me to thank you run away,

21
00:02:39,083 --> 00:02:40,903
or do you want to fight?

22
00:02:42,103 --> 00:02:44,820
Hmm if we break down what
just happened It's one of

23
00:02:44,903 --> 00:02:47,500
those knight in shining armor
saves the princess moments,

24
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:48,413
huh?

25
00:02:48,496 --> 00:02:51,160
You could burst into tears
and throw your arms around me.

26
00:02:51,243 --> 00:02:52,623
Oh, piss off, loser.

27
00:02:53,603 --> 00:02:55,023
Nah, I was just kidding.

28
00:02:56,703 --> 00:02:57,583
No way!

29
00:02:58,063 --> 00:03:01,583
It won't let her do that!
Watch it! Stay out of sight.

30
00:03:01,943 --> 00:03:04,620
Mommy and me are the only
ones allowed to hug Daddy.

31
00:03:04,703 --> 00:03:05,663
Wait, Daddy?

32
00:03:06,623 --> 00:03:08,223
What? Nothing. No.

33
00:03:08,823 --> 00:03:09,723
No way.

34
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:12,241
Is that one of those private pixies?

35
00:03:13,203 --> 00:03:14,983
Sort of, I guess.

36
00:03:15,763 --> 00:03:16,863
Mm-hmm.

37
00:03:17,663 --> 00:03:22,545
Then how about you tell me what a Spriggan
like you is doing wandering around here?

38
00:03:22,663 --> 00:03:24,743
I guess I got lost.

39
00:03:28,663 --> 00:03:30,583
How could you get that lost?

40
00:03:31,163 --> 00:03:33,339
Spriggan territory's way to the east.

41
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:34,903
God, you're weird.

42
00:03:39,783 --> 00:03:41,683
Anyway, thank you for saving me.

43
00:03:42,103 --> 00:03:43,600
I guess I should introduce myself.

44
00:03:43,683 --> 00:03:45,483
I'm Leafa. Nice to meet you.

45
00:03:45,823 --> 00:03:48,343
I'm Kirito, and this is Yui.

46
00:03:53,623 --> 00:03:55,643
Okay, then, Kirito.

47
00:03:56,063 --> 00:03:57,710
Do you have any plans today?

48
00:03:57,963 --> 00:04:01,683
I mean, because if you don't, I
can buy you a drink as thanks.

49
00:04:02,503 --> 00:04:03,640
A drink sounds awesome.

50
00:04:03,723 --> 00:04:07,020
And if you don't mind, I'd like to
pick your brain about some stuff.

51
00:04:07,103 --> 00:04:08,574
Like, what kind of stuff?

52
00:04:08,703 --> 00:04:13,103
Just more about this world,
and especially about the tree.

53
00:04:13,603 --> 00:04:15,723
Oh, you mean the world tree?

54
00:04:17,343 --> 00:04:18,173
Yeah, sure.

55
00:04:18,303 --> 00:04:21,774
I might not look like it, but
I know a lot about this game.

56
00:04:22,163 --> 00:04:24,620
There's this neutral
village to the north of us.

57
00:04:24,703 --> 00:04:27,060
It's a little out of the
way, but we can fly there.

58
00:04:27,143 --> 00:04:29,283
Okay, but what about Sylvain?

59
00:04:29,483 --> 00:04:31,189
Isn't that town closer to us?

60
00:04:31,703 --> 00:04:34,360
You really don't know
anything about this game.

61
00:04:34,443 --> 00:04:36,703
Sylvain is sylph territory. So?

62
00:04:37,063 --> 00:04:38,100
You're not a sylph.

63
00:04:38,183 --> 00:04:40,220
If you're in their territory,
you can't attack them.

64
00:04:40,303 --> 00:04:41,723
But they can attack you.

65
00:04:43,203 --> 00:04:46,640
As long as I don't do anything to
provoke them, no one will attack me.

66
00:04:46,723 --> 00:04:48,605
And you'll be there, Miss Leafa.

67
00:04:49,923 --> 00:04:51,103
Just call me Leafa.

68
00:04:51,383 --> 00:04:53,900
And if you really want to
go there, I'll take you.

69
00:04:53,983 --> 00:04:56,218
I can't guarantee your safety, though.

70
00:04:57,103 --> 00:04:58,103
Let's get flying.

71
00:05:02,263 --> 00:05:07,223
Wait, you mean you can fly without using
the controller? Of course. Can't you?

72
00:05:07,503 --> 00:05:11,100
I just learned how to use this thing, so
I'm still trying to figure everything out.

73
00:05:11,183 --> 00:05:13,883
Well, there's a little trick to doing it.

74
00:05:14,343 --> 00:05:17,100
Come on, turn around, but
don't access your controller.

75
00:05:17,183 --> 00:05:18,013
OK.

76
00:05:19,263 --> 00:05:21,460
Can you feel where my
hand is touching you?

77
00:05:21,543 --> 00:05:22,373
Mm-hmm.

78
00:05:22,456 --> 00:05:26,180
Imagine you've got virtual bones and
muscles here, spreading out into your wings.

79
00:05:26,263 --> 00:05:27,500
Then try and move them.

80
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:29,423
Virtual bones and muscles.

81
00:05:31,643 --> 00:05:33,203
Yeah, just like that.

82
00:05:34,783 --> 00:05:35,823
You got it!

83
00:05:36,463 --> 00:05:39,169
OK, now try doing the
same thing, only harder.

84
00:05:54,763 --> 00:05:58,763
Oh no! Daddy! Gidito! Are you okay?

85
00:06:06,683 --> 00:06:09,143
How do I make it stop?

86
00:06:14,203 --> 00:06:15,783
Daddy, that's hilarious!

87
00:06:26,183 --> 00:06:28,683
Wow, this is awesome! I know, right?

88
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:32,805
Looks like you're starting
to get the hang of it!

89
00:06:32,923 --> 00:06:35,303
Now, follow me! Okay!

90
00:06:35,923 --> 00:06:38,276
Take it slow until you get better at it!

91
00:06:39,623 --> 00:06:41,043
Don't worry about me!

92
00:06:41,183 --> 00:06:42,263
We can go faster.

93
00:06:44,043 --> 00:06:44,873
Okay.

94
00:06:55,463 --> 00:06:56,293
Huh?

95
00:06:56,383 --> 00:06:58,148
Is that as fast as you can go?

96
00:06:58,943 --> 00:07:00,590
Don't blame me if you crash.

97
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:15,303
I can't go on! I need a break!

98
00:07:23,583 --> 00:07:27,465
You're the only person I know who
can handle flying at this speed!

99
00:07:35,603 --> 00:07:36,503
We made it!

100
00:07:37,743 --> 00:07:41,331
Hey, we're gonna land at the
base of the central tower, okay?

101
00:07:41,823 --> 00:07:44,943
Wait, Kirito, you do
know how to land, right?

102
00:07:46,403 --> 00:07:47,683
No, not really.

103
00:07:49,043 --> 00:07:49,873
Uh...

104
00:07:49,956 --> 00:07:50,823
Oh, crap.

105
00:07:51,183 --> 00:07:52,183
Too late now.

106
00:07:52,663 --> 00:07:53,963
You're on your own.

107
00:07:54,263 --> 00:07:55,203
Wait, what?

108
00:07:55,463 --> 00:07:56,663
You're kidding me!

109
00:08:04,523 --> 00:08:06,443
That was so not cool.

110
00:08:06,883 --> 00:08:09,223
Stop whining already, I can heal you.

111
00:08:10,803 --> 00:08:13,323
Sue, Fila, Haedal, Astolu.

112
00:08:16,383 --> 00:08:17,423
No way!

113
00:08:17,783 --> 00:08:18,823
This is magic?

114
00:08:19,143 --> 00:08:23,140
The Undine are the only ones who
specialize in high-level healing spells.

115
00:08:23,223 --> 00:08:26,600
But that's an important one anyone
can do, so you should learn it.

116
00:08:26,683 --> 00:08:29,212
Different races have
different skills, huh?

117
00:08:30,323 --> 00:08:32,800
Does the Spriggan race have
anything they're good at?

118
00:08:32,883 --> 00:08:36,540
Well, you guys are good at treasure
hunting and illusion magic.

119
00:08:36,623 --> 00:08:39,917
Neither of those things are
much help in battle, though.

120
00:08:46,383 --> 00:08:48,223
So this is a sylph town.

121
00:08:49,043 --> 00:08:50,403
Man, it's beautiful.

122
00:08:50,903 --> 00:08:51,963
I know, right?

123
00:08:53,303 --> 00:08:54,133
Lipa!

124
00:08:55,303 --> 00:08:56,723
Thank God you're okay!

125
00:08:57,483 --> 00:08:58,483
Oh, hey, Recon.

126
00:08:59,683 --> 00:09:01,123
I knew you'd survive!

127
00:09:02,503 --> 00:09:03,333
Sprengan!

128
00:09:04,723 --> 00:09:05,923
No, it's okay.

129
00:09:06,203 --> 00:09:08,262
He saved me from those salamanders.

130
00:09:09,223 --> 00:09:10,120
This is my friend.

131
00:09:10,203 --> 00:09:11,223
His name's Recon.

132
00:09:11,883 --> 00:09:12,713
Hey there.

133
00:09:12,803 --> 00:09:13,863
My name's Kirito.

134
00:09:14,363 --> 00:09:16,243
Oh, hi. Nice to meet you.

135
00:09:17,543 --> 00:09:19,308
Wait, what am I talking about?

136
00:09:19,403 --> 00:09:20,300
I take that back.

137
00:09:20,383 --> 00:09:21,460
You sure about him?

138
00:09:21,543 --> 00:09:23,367
He could be a spy or something.

139
00:09:23,783 --> 00:09:24,863
No, he's cool.

140
00:09:25,143 --> 00:09:28,420
I'm pretty sure if he really was
a spy, he wouldn't be such a diss.

141
00:09:28,503 --> 00:09:29,843
Gee, thanks a lot.

142
00:09:30,383 --> 00:09:33,480
Anyway, Sigurd and the others are
waiting for you at the tavern.

143
00:09:33,563 --> 00:09:34,563
Oh, that's right.

144
00:09:37,463 --> 00:09:40,223
On second thought, I can't go today. Huh?

145
00:09:40,783 --> 00:09:42,443
You're not going? Nope.

146
00:09:42,663 --> 00:09:46,192
I sort of promised Kirito I'd
buy him a drink for saving me.

147
00:09:46,403 --> 00:09:47,233
See you later.

148
00:09:47,323 --> 00:09:48,153
Wait.

149
00:09:48,236 --> 00:09:49,066
You don't have to.

150
00:09:51,143 --> 00:09:51,973
Lipa.

151
00:10:04,683 --> 00:10:06,580
Is that retcon guy your boyfriend?

152
00:10:06,663 --> 00:10:08,220
Yeah, are the two of you in love?

153
00:10:08,303 --> 00:10:09,133
No!

154
00:10:09,216 --> 00:10:10,223
We're not in love.

155
00:10:10,463 --> 00:10:13,563
We're just in the same
party is all. I don't know.

156
00:10:13,783 --> 00:10:15,560
From where I was standing,
you guys seem tight.

157
00:10:15,643 --> 00:10:16,473
Whatever.

158
00:10:16,556 --> 00:10:17,600
I know him in real life.

159
00:10:17,683 --> 00:10:20,760
We go to the same school and
we're classmates, but that's it.

160
00:10:20,843 --> 00:10:21,673
Mm-hmm.

161
00:10:23,383 --> 00:10:24,213
Ahem.

162
00:10:24,663 --> 00:10:25,823
Anyway, bottoms up.

163
00:10:26,223 --> 00:10:28,047
And thanks again for saving me.

164
00:10:32,623 --> 00:10:35,460
Those guys in the forest
were playing pretty rough.

165
00:10:35,543 --> 00:10:37,980
Are Gangs of PKers normal
for this game or what?

166
00:10:38,063 --> 00:10:41,300
Well, for one thing, the Salamander
and Sylph races never got along.

167
00:10:41,383 --> 00:10:45,360
But those guys were organized, and
that wasn't happening until recently.

168
00:10:45,443 --> 00:10:46,273
I don't know.

169
00:10:46,383 --> 00:10:50,040
If you ask me, they're gearing up
to try to clear the World Tree soon.

170
00:10:50,123 --> 00:10:53,500
Actually, I was hoping you could tell
me what you knew about the World Tree.

171
00:10:53,583 --> 00:10:55,540
Oh, yeah, you mentioned it before.

172
00:10:55,623 --> 00:10:56,580
Why do you want to know?

173
00:10:56,663 --> 00:10:59,203
I want to get to the top as soon as I can.

174
00:11:00,543 --> 00:11:01,443
Join the club.

175
00:11:01,683 --> 00:11:03,500
Every player wants to get to the top.

176
00:11:03,583 --> 00:11:06,818
You could say that's the
grand quest of Alfheim Online.

177
00:11:07,103 --> 00:11:08,103
What do you mean?

178
00:11:08,643 --> 00:11:11,340
You know how you're limited
in how high you can fly?

179
00:11:11,423 --> 00:11:12,253
The fact is,

180
00:11:12,336 --> 00:11:16,140
none of the races can fly continuously
for more than 10 minutes at a time.

181
00:11:16,223 --> 00:11:17,053
However,

182
00:11:17,136 --> 00:11:21,864
at the top of the tree is the floating city,
and in it lives Oberon, the Fairy King.

183
00:11:22,323 --> 00:11:24,440
The first race to reach him will be reborn

184
00:11:24,523 --> 00:11:27,170
as an advanced class of
fairy known as Alphs.

185
00:11:27,463 --> 00:11:29,500
And what's cool about that is they'll be

186
00:11:29,583 --> 00:11:31,960
able to fly around for
as long as they want.

187
00:11:32,043 --> 00:11:32,923
That is cool.

188
00:11:33,363 --> 00:11:35,892
It'd be sweet to fly
for as long as I want.

189
00:11:37,183 --> 00:11:39,948
So how does someone get
to the top of the tree?

190
00:11:40,223 --> 00:11:42,600
At the base of the tree,
there's a big dome.

191
00:11:42,683 --> 00:11:44,780
That's the gateway to the floating city.

192
00:11:44,863 --> 00:11:49,628
But then you have to get past the NPCs
that guard it, and they're super powerful.

193
00:11:49,723 --> 00:11:51,194
They're that strong, huh?

194
00:11:51,623 --> 00:11:52,720
Let me put it this way.

195
00:11:52,803 --> 00:11:54,860
The game's been around
for a year now, right?

196
00:11:54,943 --> 00:11:56,323
No one's got past them.

197
00:11:57,063 --> 00:11:59,420
Maybe everyone's missed
that one key quest.

198
00:11:59,503 --> 00:12:00,333
No, wait.

199
00:12:00,603 --> 00:12:04,015
Maybe it's designed so that
one race can't reach it alone.

200
00:12:04,903 --> 00:12:06,763
Hey, you got good instincts.

201
00:12:07,103 --> 00:12:09,740
For now, everyone seems to
think it's a missing quest,

202
00:12:09,823 --> 00:12:11,260
so they're out there looking for it.

203
00:12:11,343 --> 00:12:14,620
But if we have to work together
to beat it, it'll never happen.

204
00:12:14,703 --> 00:12:15,533
Why not?

205
00:12:15,903 --> 00:12:17,668
Because it doesn't make sense.

206
00:12:17,823 --> 00:12:21,980
Why would you help another race with a quest
if they're the ones who get the reward?

207
00:12:22,063 --> 00:12:25,300
Can you imagine anyone being
cool with that arrangement?

208
00:12:25,383 --> 00:12:28,383
Then, getting to the top
of the tree is impossible.

209
00:12:28,663 --> 00:12:30,545
What's the point in even trying?

210
00:12:31,243 --> 00:12:32,543
No arguments here.

211
00:12:34,263 --> 00:12:36,322
Flying is pretty addictive, though.

212
00:12:36,483 --> 00:12:38,680
Once you get a taste for
it, you can't give it up.

213
00:12:38,763 --> 00:12:41,503
You think, even if it
takes years, someday.

214
00:12:41,843 --> 00:12:43,843
But I can't wait around that long!

215
00:12:50,523 --> 00:12:51,353
Daddy?

216
00:12:53,123 --> 00:12:53,953
Sorry.

217
00:12:54,123 --> 00:12:58,535
It's just that I have to get to the
top of the world tree as soon as I can.

218
00:13:00,463 --> 00:13:01,293
Okay.

219
00:13:01,376 --> 00:13:02,423
What's the rush?

220
00:13:02,663 --> 00:13:05,023
I'm sort of looking for someone.

221
00:13:05,603 --> 00:13:06,603
What do you mean?

222
00:13:07,483 --> 00:13:10,143
No offense, but it's hard to explain.

223
00:13:17,423 --> 00:13:18,480
Thank you, Leafa.

224
00:13:18,563 --> 00:13:21,269
All the info you gave
me is really gonna help.

225
00:13:28,083 --> 00:13:28,913
Wait.

226
00:13:28,996 --> 00:13:31,290
Are you heading for the
World Tree right now?

227
00:13:32,023 --> 00:13:32,853
Uh-huh.

228
00:13:33,023 --> 00:13:34,494
I need to see for myself.

229
00:13:37,723 --> 00:13:38,553
Alone?

230
00:13:38,683 --> 00:13:39,540
That's crazy.

231
00:13:39,623 --> 00:13:43,505
It's really far away and you'll
have to fight a bunch of monsters?

232
00:13:43,803 --> 00:13:45,440
I know you can handle yourself,

233
00:13:45,523 --> 00:13:51,323
but hey if you want I can take you there?

234
00:13:55,463 --> 00:13:56,293
Thanks,

235
00:13:56,376 --> 00:14:00,100
but we just met and I wouldn't feel
right you coming all that way right then?

236
00:14:00,183 --> 00:14:01,600
maybe you already know how to get there.

237
00:14:01,683 --> 00:14:04,095
What you're gonna do about the guardians?

238
00:14:04,183 --> 00:14:07,083
Well, I'll think of
something when I get there

239
00:14:08,043 --> 00:14:10,663
Too late my mind's made up

240
00:14:13,843 --> 00:14:14,673
Okay.

241
00:14:16,483 --> 00:14:18,601
So, do you want to meet up tomorrow?

242
00:14:18,823 --> 00:14:19,683
Yeah, sure.

243
00:14:20,123 --> 00:14:21,960
Then I'll meet you here
tomorrow at 3 p .m.

244
00:14:22,043 --> 00:14:22,873
sharp.

245
00:14:22,956 --> 00:14:23,992
Um, I have to log out now.

246
00:14:24,103 --> 00:14:26,980
So when you're ready, you can log out
in one of the rooms upstairs, okay?

247
00:14:27,063 --> 00:14:29,003
Well, see you then. Uh, wait!

248
00:14:33,783 --> 00:14:34,783
Thank you, Leafa.

249
00:14:43,303 --> 00:14:44,133
You

250
00:14:58,083 --> 00:15:00,663
Hey, if you want I can take you there?

251
00:15:09,883 --> 00:15:11,863
Talk about a weird guy!

252
00:15:14,343 --> 00:15:15,503
Hmm. Kirito.

253
00:15:25,723 --> 00:15:28,943
I guess this means goodbye
till tomorrow, doesn't it?

254
00:15:29,263 --> 00:15:30,840
Yeah, but I'll be back soon.

255
00:15:30,923 --> 00:15:32,217
It won't be that long.

256
00:15:34,983 --> 00:15:35,813
Daddy?

257
00:15:35,896 --> 00:15:38,263
Would it be alright if
I slept next to you?

258
00:15:38,643 --> 00:15:40,403
Just until you log out?

259
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:45,083
